      "title": "radiotap: improve display of 0-length PSDU frames",
      "message": "radiotap: improve display of 0-length PSDU frames\n\nThe \"Info\" column just always shows the radiotap data,\nwhich isn't very useful. Show the 0-length PSDU type\nand, if present, the \"bad PLCP\" indication instead.\n\nAlso fix the 0-len PSDU type 1 to say \"data not captured\"\nas the radiotap spec specifies.\n\nAssisted-by: GitHub Copilot\n",
